messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 99 and 31?', "<think>\nTo find the product of 99 and 31, I can use the distributive property to simplify the multiplication.\n\nFirst, I'll break down 99 into 100 minus 1. This makes the multiplication easier.\n\nNext, I'll multiply both parts of the broken-down number by 31. So, 100 times 31 is 3100, and 1 times 31 is 31.\n\nFinally, I'll subtract the second result from the first to get the final product.\n. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
response:  {
  "id": "cmpl-348d63e50a214d5780cbbdf77c4dd691",
  "object": "text_completion",
  "created": 1754619987,
  "model": "DeepSeekR1-Qwen-7B",
  "choices": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "3089.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **99** and **31**, we can use the distributive property to simplify the multiplication. Here's a step-by-step solution:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n99 \\times 31 &= (100 - 1) \\times 31 \\\\\n&= 100 \\times 31 - 1 \\times 31 \\\\\n&= 3100 - 31 \\\\\n&= 3089\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\\[\n\\boxed{3089}\n\\]",
      "logprobs": null,
      "finish_reason": "stop",
      "stop_reason": null,
