      "index": 0,
      "text": "7919.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **99** and **81**, we can use the distributive property to simplify the multiplication. Here's a step-by-step solution:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n99 \\times 81 &= (100 - 1) \\times 81 \\\\\n&= 100 \\times 81 - 1 \\times 81 \\\\\n&= 8100 - 81 \\\\\n&= 7919\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{7919}\n\\]",
