[['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 62 and 72?', "<think>.\nTo find the product of 62 and 72, I'll start by breaking down each number into tens and ones.\n\nFirst, I'll express 62 as 60 plus 2, and 72 as 70 plus 2.\n\nNext, I'll use the distributive property to multiply these components:.\n(60 + 2) × (70 + 2) = 60×70 + 60×2 + 2×70 + 2×2.\n\nNow, I'll calculate each part:.\n60 multiplied by 70 is 4200,.\n60 multiplied by 2 is 120,.\n2 multiplied by 70 is 140,.\nand 2 multiplied by 2 is 4.\n\nFinally, I'll add all these results together:. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
